{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Cancel Effects","roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()"},{"text":" and the store’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all-or-nothing"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"cancel id"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"text":" effect or the imperative ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"text":" method. Identity lives outside the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Choosing an id","level":2,"anchor":"Choosing-an-id"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A cancel id is any ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable & Sendable"},{"text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","level":2,"anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Return ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"text":" to tag the work, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"text":" to stop it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","level":2,"anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Passing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancelInFlight: true"},{"text":" cancels any effect already running under the id ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".queryChanged"},{"text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancel from view or scene code","level":2,"anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"text":" directly:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What it does not replace","level":2,"anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"text":" continuation should still release it — use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defer"},{"text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"else"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" has to stop the effect early.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"How-to Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancel(id:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Cancels every in-flight effect tagged with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" via","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/cancel(id:)","title":"cancel(id:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancelEffects()":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/canceleffects()","title":"cancelEffects()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels all in-flight effects."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancelEffects"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Add a Parental Gate","identifi